{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rf5wbpcoiekdfsczf5cfxftnw4vi5ln2n7ztauiv5i6a2kwqo3ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent finding — note that **no Rust build appears in the mismatch list**. The divergences are between the C's own `-O` levels, purely in unspecified NaN sign bits. Let me make the test assert exactly that:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2227,"cache_read_input_tokens":240401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2227,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28b3df08-e114-40c6-835f-7a4bcdb69832","uuid":"3f84033c-c2c9-492d-a49d-362053aae7de","timestamp":"2026-08-26T23:12:33.656Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rf5wbpcoiekdfsczf5cfxftnw4vi5ln2n7ztauiv5i6a2kwqo3ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01QEo8xsKf8w5x2SkCSKKVsM","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QX18IK/translation/tests/optlevels.rs","old_string":"//! `target/`) and requires *all* of them to agree with each other and with the\n//! Rust `.so`, bit for bit.\n//!\n//! `-ffast-math` is deliberately NOT tested: it licenses the compiler to break\n//! IEEE-754 semantics, so it would be a different program.","new_string":"//! `target/`) and compares all of them.\n//!\n//! **Result of running it:** the Rust matches the CMake-built C on every input,\n//! but the C's *own* optimisation levels do not all agree with each other. Every\n//! such disagreement is confined to the **sign and payload bits of a NaN** — a\n//! value IEEE-754 leaves unspecified and which gcc's instruction selection\n//! therefore changes freely (at `-O0` `fabsf` is a real `andps 0x7fffffff` that\n//! clears the sign; at `-O1`+ gcc folds it away and the original NaN sign\n//! survives). So this test asserts the two things that are actually true and\n//! meaningful:\n//!\n//!   1. the Rust reproduces the CMake-built C **bit for bit, always** (that build\n//!      is the ground truth named by the task), and\n//!   2. wherever the C's behaviour is *optimisation-independent*, the Rust agrees\n//!      with it too — i.e. every remaining disagreement is NaN-vs-NaN, never a\n//!      difference in a numeric value, a zero sign, or which branch was taken.\n//!\n//! `-ffast-math` is deliberately NOT tested: it licenses the compiler to break\n//! IEEE-754 semantics, so it would be a different program."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2227,"cache_read_input_tokens":240401,"cache_creation":{"ep